        "content": "<p>ColonelToad opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14942\">PR #14942</a> from <code>ColonelToad:fix/14691-riscv64-swizzle-splat-zext</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #14691.</p>\n<p><code>vrgather.vx</code> uses the full scalar register as the vector index, but the upper bits of an i8/i16/i32 value are not guaranteed to be zero. Zero-extend the splat index before lowering so out-of-range upper bits cannot change the result.</p>\n<p>Added RISC-V ISA expectations and a runtime regression test using a dirty upper byte.</p>\n<p>Tests:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>cargo run -p cranelift-tools -- test cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/riscv64/simd-swizzle.clif</li>\n<li>cargo run -p cranelift-tools -- test cranelift/filetests/filetests/runtests/simd-swizzle.clif</li>\n<li>cargo fmt --all -- --check</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The RISC-V runtime portion is covered by the QEMU CI job.</p>\n</blockquote>",
